Arduino software tests
======================

From the repository root, with Python 3 and Clang installed:

    python3 test/test_arduino_library.py -v
    python3 test/test_midi_example.py -v

These commands compile the actual portable library and MIDI example using
AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer. They require no firmware
binaries, external recovered C code, Arduino hardware or Python packages.
On macOS the runners use the Xcode SDK when a full Xcode installation exists.

The native checks exercise protocol, display, events, publication, queue and
MIDI behavior. Hardware SPI timing and actual panel compatibility are not
covered. Please report physical test results in a GitHub issue.

AVR compilation:

    pio run -e uno -e mega2560 -e uno_midi

Use sh tools/build_arduino_docker.sh if the AVR toolchain cannot execute on
your host. See docs/arduino-library.md for validation limits.
